# Pin working-tree and committed text to LF. Without this file, every
# checkout follows the machine's `core.autocrlf`. Git for Windows defaults
# that to `true`, so a contributor inherits a tree where every first-party
# text file is rewritten from this repository's LF to CRLF, and the
# corruption does not announce itself as a line-ending problem (Pint
# `line_ending` fixers, YAML/frontmatter parsers seeing `\r`, line-based
# tests). A committed `eol=lf` outranks `core.autocrlf`.
#
# `text=auto` still detects binary content and leaves it alone. Repositories
# may add more specific lines under this (diff drivers, `export-ignore`,
# `merge=union` for an append-only decision log); keep this line first.
* text=auto eol=lf

/* export-ignore
/.* export-ignore
/inc -export-ignore
/admin -export-ignore
/assets -export-ignore
/uamswp-shortcodes.php -export-ignore

# An append-only log: two branches that each add an entry keep both sides. The order
# check (`.claude/skills/decision-log`) catches the misordering and lost separator this can cause.
docs/DECISIONS.md merge=union
